{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a068945cd37e429267c977","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"dspy Tool kwargs \"VAR_KEYWORD\" pull request \"dspy/primitives/tool.py\" **kwargs support\"\n\nHere are the search results for your query:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. **[Bug] Tool calling kwargs — Issue #7910 (stanfordnlp/dspy)** ⭐ Most Relevant\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/issues/7910\n\nThis is the core issue behind the `VAR_KEYWORD` / `**kwargs` support in dspy's Tool class:\n\n- **Reporter:** @ButterflyAtHeart (opened Mar 5, 2025; closed Apr 26, 2025 by @chenmoneygithub)\n- **Problem:** When calling tools with a ReAct agent, the model sometimes predicts `next_tool_args` as `{\"foo\": \"bar\"}` instead of `{\"kwargs\": {\"foo\": \"bar\"}}` for functions defined with `**kwargs`, raising `ValueError: Arg foo is not in the tool's args.`\n- **Repro:** `dspy.Tool(func=lambda **kwargs: \"Completed.\", name=\"finish\", args={})` then calling `f(foo=\"bar\")` fails.\n- **Proposed fix (by reporter):** Check for `_ParameterKind.VAR_KEYWORD` in the signature (around line 88 of tools.py), set a new `Tool` instance variable, and use it to adjust `Tool.__call__`.\n- **Resolution:** @chenmoneygithub confirmed \"This is supported now,\" pointing to `dspy/primitives/tool.py` (line 61 at commit `6ee8cdca`), and closed the issue.\n\n### 2. **dspy/adapters/types/tool.py** (current implementation)\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/blob/77cb2331/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py\n\nThe fix as it exists today (Tool moved to `adapters/types/`), showing the `has_kwargs` mechanism:\n\n```python\nhas_kwargs: bool = False\n...\nself.has_kwargs = any(param.kind == param.VAR_KEYWORD for param in sig.parameters.values())\n\ndef _validate_and_parse_args(self, **kwargs):\n    for k, v in kwargs.items():\n        if k not in self.args:\n            if self.has_kwargs:\n                continue   # allow arbitrary kwargs\n            else:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Arg {k} is not in the tool's args.\")\n```\n\nA nearly identical version exists at commit 2974a655.\n\n### 3. **dspy.Tool API docs**\n**URL:** https://dspy.ai/api/primitives/Tool/\n\nDocuments `__call__(**kwargs)` which routes through `_validate_and_parse_args` before invoking `self.func`.\n\n### 4. **PR #9341 — fix(interpreter): Harden JSONRPC communication and tool bridge** (related, but different)\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/pull/9341\n\nA merged PR touching tool-calling behavior in the interpreter/sandbox bridge — it *removes* `*args, **kwargs` fallback for untyped tools there (\"Tools with *args or *kwargs are not supported\" in that specific bridge context), which is distinct from the `Tool` class `has_kwargs` support above.\n\n**Summary:** The `VAR_KEYWORD` support you're looking for originated in issue #7910 and was implemented via the `has_kwargs` check in the Tool class (originally in `dspy/primitives/tool.py`, later `dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`), allowing tools with `**kwargs` signatures to accept arbitrary keyword arguments without raising validation errors.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"919e1a27-296c-4b52-a99d-24b9ce88abc3","uuid":"aeed339b-beab-48fd-94b3-b6f5a52bba8b","timestamp":"2026-09-03T18:43:14.365Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"dspy Tool kwargs \"VAR_KEYWORD\" pull request \"dspy/primitives/tool.py\" **kwargs support","results":["Here are the search results for your query:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. **[Bug] Tool calling kwargs — Issue #7910 (stanfordnlp/dspy)** ⭐ Most Relevant\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/issues/7910\n\nThis is the core issue behind the `VAR_KEYWORD` / `**kwargs` support in dspy's Tool class:\n\n- **Reporter:** @ButterflyAtHeart (opened Mar 5, 2025; closed Apr 26, 2025 by @chenmoneygithub)\n- **Problem:** When calling tools with a ReAct agent, the model sometimes predicts `next_tool_args` as `{\"foo\": \"bar\"}` instead of `{\"kwargs\": {\"foo\": \"bar\"}}` for functions defined with `**kwargs`, raising `ValueError: Arg foo is not in the tool's args.`\n- **Repro:** `dspy.Tool(func=lambda **kwargs: \"Completed.\", name=\"finish\", args={})` then calling `f(foo=\"bar\")` fails.\n- **Proposed fix (by reporter):** Check for `_ParameterKind.VAR_KEYWORD` in the signature (around line 88 of tools.py), set a new `Tool` instance variable, and use it to adjust `Tool.__call__`.\n- **Resolution:** @chenmoneygithub confirmed \"This is supported now,\" pointing to `dspy/primitives/tool.py` (line 61 at commit `6ee8cdca`), and closed the issue.\n\n### 2. **dspy/adapters/types/tool.py** (current implementation)\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/blob/77cb2331/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py\n\nThe fix as it exists today (Tool moved to `adapters/types/`), showing the `has_kwargs` mechanism:\n\n```python\nhas_kwargs: bool = False\n...\nself.has_kwargs = any(param.kind == param.VAR_KEYWORD for param in sig.parameters.values())\n\ndef _validate_and_parse_args(self, **kwargs):\n    for k, v in kwargs.items():\n        if k not in self.args:\n            if self.has_kwargs:\n                continue   # allow arbitrary kwargs\n            else:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Arg {k} is not in the tool's args.\")\n```\n\nA nearly identical version exists at commit 2974a655.\n\n### 3. **dspy.Tool API docs**\n**URL:** https://dspy.ai/api/primitives/Tool/\n\nDocuments `__call__(**kwargs)` which routes through `_validate_and_parse_args` before invoking `self.func`.\n\n### 4. **PR #9341 — fix(interpreter): Harden JSONRPC communication and tool bridge** (related, but different)\n**URL:** https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/pull/9341\n\nA merged PR touching tool-calling behavior in the interpreter/sandbox bridge — it *removes* `*args, **kwargs` fallback for untyped tools there (\"Tools with *args or *kwargs are not supported\" in that specific bridge context), which is distinct from the `Tool` class `has_kwargs` support above.\n\n**Summary:** The `VAR_KEYWORD` support you're looking for originated in issue #7910 and was implemented via the `has_kwargs` check in the Tool class (originally in `dspy/primitives/tool.py`, later `dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`), allowing tools with `**kwargs` signatures to accept arbitrary keyword arguments without raising validation errors."],"durationSeconds":45.353179834999985,"searchCount":1}}
